{"code":"47-2111.00","title":"Electricians","description":"Install, maintain, and repair electrical wiring, equipment, and fixtures. Ensure that work is in accordance with relevant codes. May install or service street lights, intercom systems, or electrical control systems.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.4934},"I":{"score":2.7,"share":0.1398},"A":{"score":1.24,"share":0.0197},"S":{"score":1.32,"share":0.0263},"E":{"score":1.81,"share":0.0666},"C":{"score":4.09,"share":0.2541}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":2882,"text":"Prepare sketches or follow blueprints to determine the location of wiring or equipment and to ensure conformance to building and safety codes.","core":true,"importance":4.63,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.46},{"id":2888,"text":"Place conduit, pipes, or tubing, inside designated partitions, walls, or other concealed areas, and pull insulated wires or cables through the conduit to complete circuits between boxes.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.43},{"id":2887,"text":"Work from ladders, scaffolds, or roofs to install, maintain, or repair electrical wiring, equipment, or fixtures.","core":true,"importance":4.55,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.91},{"id":2883,"text":"Use a variety of tools or equipment, such as power construction equipment, measuring devices, power tools, and testing equipment, such as oscilloscopes, ammeters, or test lamps.","core":true,"importance":4.52,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.95},{"id":2873,"text":"Assemble, install, test, or maintain electrical or electronic wiring, equipment, appliances, apparatus, or fixtures, using hand tools or power tools.","core":true,"importance":4.45,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.54},{"id":2875,"text":"Connect wires to circuit breakers, transformers, or other components.","core":true,"importance":4.31,"relevance":99.07,"frequency":4.76},{"id":2879,"text":"Maintain current electrician's license or identification card to meet governmental regulations.","core":true,"importance":4.31,"relevance":89.79,"frequency":2.98},{"id":2880,"text":"Plan layout and installation of electrical wiring, equipment, or fixtures, based on job specifications and local codes.","core":true,"importance":4.21,"relevance":99.88,"frequency":4.77},{"id":2878,"text":"Test electrical systems or continuity of circuits in electrical wiring, equipment, or fixtures, using testing devices, such as ohmmeters, voltmeters, or oscilloscopes, to ensure compatibility and safety of system.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.52},{"id":2881,"text":"Direct or train workers to install, maintain, or repair electrical wiring, equipment, or fixtures.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":90.54,"frequency":4.8},{"id":2874,"text":"Diagnose malfunctioning systems, apparatus, or components, using test equipment and hand tools to locate the cause of a breakdown and correct the problem.","core":true,"importance":4.01,"relevance":99.76,"frequency":4.25},{"id":2876,"text":"Inspect electrical systems, equipment, or components to identify hazards, defects, or the need for adjustment or repair, and to ensure compliance with codes.","core":true,"importance":3.98,"relevance":97.85,"frequency":4.5},{"id":2884,"text":"Install ground leads and connect power cables to equipment, such as motors.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":96.79,"frequency":4},{"id":2877,"text":"Advise management on whether continued operation of equipment could be hazardous.","core":true,"importance":3.92,"relevance":78.04,"frequency":3.04},{"id":2886,"text":"Repair or replace wiring, equipment, or fixtures, using hand tools or power tools.","core":true,"importance":3.92,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.52},{"id":20439,"text":"Construct or fabricate parts, using hand tools, according to specifications.","core":true,"importance":3.89,"relevance":90.67,"frequency":4.26},{"id":2893,"text":"Provide assistance during emergencies by operating floodlights or generators, placing flare